.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Christian Samuel Weiss (1815) sorted crystals into systems by the lengths of, and angles between, their crystallographic axes -- the idea that survives as today&#x27;s 7 crystal systems. classify_crystal_system classifies a unit cell purely from the equalities/inequalities among its six lattice parameters (a,b,c,\alpha,\beta,\gamma), and unit_cell_volume gives the general-cell volume formula that reduces to familiar shortcuts (abc, \frac{\sqrt3}{2}a^2c) in special cases.">

